11. R² as a Diagnostic
Wermers (2011) notes that managed long-only portfolios typically have \(R^2 &gt; 90\%\) under the Carhart model, precisely because these four factors capture most passive variation. Low \(R^2\) signals idiosyncratic strategies not captured by the standard factors.


